Getting started
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

folio renders Markdown in the terminal with italic, bold italic, strikethrough
and `inline code`. Links look like the docs (https://example.com/docs), and bare
URLs like https://example.com stay readable. Anchors such as the install section
don't repeat their target.

Install
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Run the installer, then check the version.[1] Each step is safe to repeat.[2]

1. Download the release.
2. Unpack it:
   ◦ on macOS, double-click the archive
   ◦ on Linux, use `tar -xzf folio.tar.gz`
     ▪ nested lists get their own bullet
3. Put `folio` on your `PATH`.

